# Fixed defect 2368, 2026-11-09, lane b26-misc, the issue's own reproducer
# (lane b26-fmt's, on a copy of `examples/todo`'s catalogue; here a `path`
# entry, whose module carries the same mark): `use other/strings` beside
# `use <core>/strings`, both binding `strings`.
#
# SYMPTOM, as lane b26-fmt measured it on the trunk's compiler before defect
# 2367's repair: the package's line was told, with `fix (guess): write
# `use <core>/strings as <core>_strings``, no name. Read in the key's order
# and by which line a fix can repair, the plain line is told, and its fix was
# already a name on this lane's base.
#
# FIX: it keeps it, `other_strings`; the package's line, were it told, would
# be offered `core_strings`.
use <core>/strings

use other/strings  #~ module_binding_taken

function main()
    print(strings.hello())
